# Assertions about individuals — the spellings DLe accepts for the ABox.
#
# This document exists to be read. It deliberately uses several spellings of the same axiom
# shape, so it does not round-trip byte for byte: the writer picks one form per kind, and
# `rex:Cat`, `ex:ada:Person` and `bob : Person` are all class assertions that come back
# spaced. What must survive is the set of axioms, which is what the CI regression job
# compares.
#
# The forms follow Introduction to Description Logic:
#
#   a : C          a is a C, where C may be any concept expression
#   (a,b):r        a is related to b by the object property r
#   ¬(a,b):r       a is not related to b by r
#   (a,v):d        a's data property d has the value v
#   ¬(a,v):d       a's d does not have the value v
#   a = b          a and b are the same individual
#   a ≠ b          a and b are different individuals
#
# A class assertion may also be written without the space — `rex:Cat` — which is the
# textbook spelling. It is read as an assertion only when the part before the colon is not a
# declared prefix, because otherwise those characters are a prefixed name. Written output
# always spaces it, so the meaning never depends on the prefix declarations.
#
# A digit-initial name in the default namespace carries its own colon, so a statement about
# one has two: `(bob,rex)::246075003`. A digit-initial class needs the space as well.
#
# Three things to know before adding to this file:
#
#  - There are no comments below this header on purpose. A comment attaches to the entity
#    named by the statement under it, and several statements here share a subject, so
#    section headings would merge into one another.
#  - This header does not survive a read either: a comment block before the first @prefix
#    is dropped. It documents the file for a human reader, not for the tool.
#  - Do not route this document through RDF. `rex = rexie = rexthedog` is one three-way
#    SameIndividual axiom, and RDF has only the binary owl:sameAs, so a .ttl detour splits
#    it in two and the axiom count this file exists to hold stops holding.
#
# Not every legal spelling is here — typed literals have no syntax yet, and the enumerated
# class `{rex, zoe}` does not survive a round trip. Both are in the issue tracker.

@ontology <http://example.org/abox-forms>
@prefix : <http://example.org/abox#>
@prefix ex: <http://example.org/other#>

Cat ⊑ Animal
Dog ⊑ Animal
Animal ⊑ ⊤
Keeper ⊑ Person
∃hasPet.⊤ ⊑ Person
⊤ ⊑ ∀hasPet.Animal
(≥1 age) ⊑ Animal
⊤ ⊑ ∀age.xsd:integer
⊤ ⊑ ∀nickname.xsd:string
⊤ ⊑ ∀weight.xsd:double
⊤ ⊑ ∀tagged.xsd:boolean
Func(age)
∃caresFor.⊤ ⊑ Keeper
⊤ ⊑ ∀caresFor.Animal
hasPet ⊑ caresFor
∃:246075003.⊤ ⊑ Animal
⊤ ⊑ ∀:118586006.xsd:integer

bob : Person
rex:Cat
ex:ada:Person
ex:zoe:ex:Keeper
bob:ex:Keeper
mia : :762705008
:111000001 : Cat
bob : Person ⊓ ¬Keeper
rex : Cat ⊔ Dog
bob : ∃hasPet.Cat
bob : ≥1 hasPet.Animal
bob : ≤3 hasPet.Animal
bob : =1 hasPet.Cat
ada : ∀hasPet.Animal
zoe : ¬Cat
rex : ⊤
mia : ¬⊥
ada : ∃hasPet.{rex}
zoe : ∃caresFor.Self
rex : ∃age.xsd:integer

(bob,rex):hasPet
(ex:ada,rex):hasPet
(ex:zoe,rex):caresFor
¬(ex:zoe,rex):hasPet
(bob,rex)::246075003
¬(mia,rex)::246075003
(:111000001,rex):hasPet

(rex,7):age
(rex,-3):age
(rex,4.5):weight
(rex,true):tagged
(rex,"Rexie"):nickname
(rex,"Rexie le chien"@fr):nickname
(rex,""):nickname
(rex,"says \"woof\""):nickname
(rex,9)::118586006
¬(bob,"Bobby"):nickname
¬(rex,3):age
¬(rex,"Rexie le chat"@fr):nickname
¬(rex,9)::118586006

bob = robert
mia ≠ zoe
rex = rexie = rexthedog
bob ≠ mia ≠ zoe
:111000001 = :111000002

@label bob "Bob"
@label ex:ada "Ada"@en
@doc rex "A dog, asserted several ways to exercise the reader."
@ann mia rdfs:seeAlso "https://example.org/mia"
